{
  "work_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus",
  "source_path": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus.json",
  "source_language": "cop",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-10-12",
      "script": "scripts.embed_eval.translate"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0002",
      "source_sha256": "91d3132a58cbacd5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He also spoke in this same encomium about the holy martyr and virgin, Apa Peter, the archbishop of this same city, Alexandria."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0012",
      "source_sha256": "bff4b1c441f37cee",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Visible rain produces visible, physical fruit."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0021",
      "source_sha256": "a616889e9c59ac62",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The fruits I mentioned earlier are these: self-control, purity, virginity, mercy, peace, hope, generosity, obedience, and the things that follow these."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0023",
      "source_sha256": "cd55ad8345fbd119",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Now is the time for me to say, with the prophet and lawgiver Moses, “Let us sing to the Lord, for he has been glorified in glory.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0059",
      "source_sha256": "0e8d9efd06c7ea72",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Do not give to him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0060",
      "source_sha256": "32306c8b820d518e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he would say to him, “My son, go and turn away from whatever sin you are committing. After that, partake of the holy mysteries.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0061",
      "source_sha256": "6de7e15f5cad7192",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So, when he continued steadfastly in this way, the whole city turned away from sins. But as [?] from sins."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0062",
      "source_sha256": "5d71a0f14cb563d4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Whenever someone saw another person committing a sin, he would rebuke him, saying, “Turn away from this deed, lest the archbishop shame you while all the people are watching you.” And that person would become afraid and stop."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0063",
      "source_sha256": "66ca0f812135116a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For this reason, many turned away and refrained from sinning."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0065",
      "source_sha256": "38ebe1b2c2a24192",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And they were all offended, and there was grumbling about him, because since Saint Mark the evangelist, no one had sat on the archbishop’s throne unless he was a virgin."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0073",
      "source_sha256": "6dbd533e35500d73",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then an angel of God appeared to him and said to him, “Demetrius, Demetrius, do not seek only your own good, but also the good of your neighbor.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0085",
      "source_sha256": "96386b79a3a94f52",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the angel had said these things to him, he disappeared from his sight."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0103",
      "source_sha256": "d75ece2d366c6711",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Listen, and marvel with me, my beloved ones."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.000.0120",
      "source_sha256": "babac92da8b53ed0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But I said to her, “If you listen to me, my sister, we will be in the place where we will never be separated from one another.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0003",
      "source_sha256": "8665dacdf0465412",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "After this, he instructed his wife to withdraw to her own place."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0010",
      "source_sha256": "1d44176c74e9684e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“Has the evil archer not shot at you?” “Yes,” he said. “I too am a human being, clothed in flesh like everyone else.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0015",
      "source_sha256": "889f9e0cd24adcd0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "I remember the ugliness of the bodies in the tombs and their stench."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0029",
      "source_sha256": "f01ed0bef4e71735",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And you are praying for us now in the place where you are. I would indeed like to speak at length with you and tell you about the wonders God performed through this holy man, Saint Demetrius, the holy archbishop."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0032",
      "source_sha256": "7ca10c7b5b1dd38c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Who, then, is this? It is Saint Peter, the archbishop of Alexandria."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0063",
      "source_sha256": "d9d4906cae55a11c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For the sake of your holy name, my Lord Jesus Christ, the Savior of my soul and my spirit, look down upon me and my two orphaned children, and have mercy on us."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0083",
      "source_sha256": "5080d93f1ec7cf62",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But when he took hold of the little children to baptize them, the baptismal font froze and became stone."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0095",
      "source_sha256": "44fd175e5e698b1b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The mother of the little children answered and said to the archbishop, “My parents and I are Christians, and I am from Antioch.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0106",
      "source_sha256": "ec0687ccc53a8f59",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But a thought came into my heart, and I took a knife in my hand."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0124",
      "source_sha256": "37e3857959675b67",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The king said to him, “Socrator, who is doing these things in Alexandria?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0126",
      "source_sha256": "cdb22a12ef85a9b2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the king heard this, he flew into a rage, because he had been angry with Saint Peter ever since he had read his discourse about the idols, which he had delivered against them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0134",
      "source_sha256": "30eaa10658cf2be7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "But she did not answer him at all."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0141",
      "source_sha256": "a055f8529fbe4872",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "The true dawn that rose from the house of David."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0143",
      "source_sha256": "bc3254b44f1a9503",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "But we know that the dawn [?], we who are in darkness and the shadow of death."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0144",
      "source_sha256": "676b378cbb471f83",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "I think, O Christ-loving assembly, that we have found the man."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/pseudo_flavianus#CopScr.pseudo-flavianus.001.0145",
      "source_sha256": "a8f94abee02bc30c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "To your love, according to the measure of our discipleship. For we ourselves are disciples of the great true teacher, our Lord, our Savior. Through him, glory be to the Father, together with him and the Holy Spirit, who gives life and is of the same essence, now and always, forever. Amen."
    }
  ]
}
